**`src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact-match via `t == tag` (not substring), order preserved (iterator order == input order).

**`src/main.rs`** — `list` now scans trailing args for `--tag <TAG>` and routes through `filter_by_tag`; without the flag it behaves exactly as before.

Verified: `cargo build` + `cargo test` (2 existing tests) pass, and a manual run of `list --tag rust`/`python`/missing returns correctly filtered, order-preserving output.


